# Vendored BMAD skill-pack installations.
#
# BMAD's installer writes the same skill pack once per AI tool it supports.
# .agents/, .agent/ and .cline/ are byte-identical copies of .claude/, and
# .opencode/ is the same content under that tool's own naming convention
# (commands/ rather than skills/). Tracking four copies of one vendored pack
# means every upstream bump lands four times in review.
#
# None of them is a canonical original — they are sibling outputs of one
# installer run, rebuilt from scratch on every `bmad install`. They are local
# dev-tool config, the same category as .venv/ or node_modules/, so none is
# versioned. All of them stay on disk so every tool keeps working.
.claude/
.agents/
.agent/
.cline/
.opencode/

# Installer-managed BMAD config.
#
# _bmad/config.toml and config.user.toml both open with "Installer-managed.
# Regenerated on every install — treat as read-only," and the module configs
# and resolver scripts are rewritten the same way. What survives an install is
# kept tracked instead: _config/manifest.yaml records which modules and
# versions to reinstall, and custom/config.toml is the team override file BMAD
# itself says to commit. Personal overrides stay out via _bmad/custom/.gitignore.
/_bmad/config.toml
/_bmad/config.user.toml
/_bmad/*/config.yaml
/_bmad/scripts/
